Add unit test framework in the project. It should run on cmake. The main goals are some of the core logic stuff pertaining to the compile engine. One major goal is to throw a massive amount of scripts at the compile engine. ones to break it, ones to check that outputs are deterministic and compiling and that compiled user code returns the results we expect, Some to check serialization and deserialization. That's the goal, but for this exact todo I want the scope to only be setting up the test framework in the project. that will include ensuring LLVM compile engine is testable, having a simple test format and folder where I can start writing unit test functions and so on. I also want a helper function specifically in the compile tests folder underneath the main test folder that specifically sets up the exact compile pipeline the app would have used, but isolated so tests can literally involve passing a source code string or a .wlsl file url from inside the testing folder, then it picks it up and compiles it. the outputs will be validated to see if they match an expected failure or an expected success. they should also return the function pointers that got compiled so we can check in the success cases if they produce valid outputs and so on